{ The third kind of rosette is an opposite rosette, (rook on) third rank, with the two kings located opposite each other. White plays one main line with two exceptions. }
1. Qf6+ Kc5 { If black had moved to the 7th rank, the rook would have been lost to a fork on f7. } (1... Kd5 2. Qf7+ Kc5 { Trapezoid position }) 2. Qe5+ Kb4 (2... Kb6 3. Kd3 Rc5 4. Qe3 Kc6 5. Kd4 Rd5+ 6. Kc4 { cage position }) 3. Kd3 { Turning the wishbone into a thorn } *


