{ The first exception to the general principle is not to use it when it would actually force the black king towards the center! Instead, attack the rook with the king and try to pivot the position clockwise. }
1. Ke3 Rd5 2. Qg8+ { skewer the king and rook } 2... Ke5 3. Qe8+ Kf6 (3... Kd6 4. Ke4 { absolute seventh extension! }) 4. Ke4 { attacking the rook with the king } 4... Rg5 { This position is part of our absolute seventh extension procedure } 5. Qf8+ Kg6 6. Kf4 *


