{ The second exception is if both of black's pieces are on the edge of the board. Giving check with the queen doesn't accomplish anything in this position, so instead give the black king one more square by backing up to e7. }
1. Qe7 Kc8 (1... Ra7 2. Qe5+ Ka8 3. Qd5+ Rb7 4. Qd8+ Ka7 5. Kc6 { Philidor position }) (1... Ra3 2. Kb6 Rb3+ 3. Ka6 Kc8 4. Qe6+ { fork }) (1... Ka8 2. Kb5 Ra2 3. Qe8+ Kb7 4. Qf7+ { fork }) 2. Kb5 { Attack the hanging rook with the king } 2... Ra1 3. Qf8+ Kc7 4. Qg7+ { fork } *


