{ This is an opposite rosette, (rook on) second rank. White has a general plan with two exceptions. }
1. Qg3 { White falls back one square on the diagonal controlling the square in front of the black king. For black, moving the king forward seems logical. } 1... Kd5 (1... Ke7 2. Kd4 { Attacking the hanging rook } 2... Rf5 3. Qc7+ Kf6 4. Ke4 Kg6 5. Qg3+ Rg5 6. Qd6+ Kh5 7. Qd7 Kh6 8. Kf4 Rg7 9. Qd6+ Kh7 10. Kf5 Rf7+ 11. Ke6 Rg7 12. Qd3+ Kg8 13. Qd4 Rg6+ 14. Ke7 Rg3 15. Qd5+ Kh7 16. Qf5+ Kg8 17. Kf6 Rg7 18. Qh5 { Philidor position }) 2. Qg5+ Kc6 3. Qe7 Rd5+ 4. Kc4 { cage position } *


