{ If the black king is on the edge of the board, our main strategy of retreating the queen one square on the diagonal eliminates any possibility of stalemate. }
1. Qd6 Kb3 2. Qb6+ Ka2 3. Qa5+ Kb1 (3... Kb3 4. Qa1 { Euwe position }) 4. Qa4 { Half Philidor } 4... Rb8 (4... Rg2 5. Qe4 Rc2 { Diagonal position } 6. Qe1+ Rc1 7. Qe5 Rc2 8. Qe4 Rb2 9. Kc3+ Ka1 10. Qe1+ Ka2 11. Qd1 { Philidor }) 5. Qe4 { Set up discovered check } 5... Rb3+ 6. Kc4+ Ka1 7. Qd4+ Ka2 8. Qd5 { Diagonal position } *


