{ The first exception to the general principle occurs when the queen is on the edge of the board and therefore retreating one square on the diagonal is not possible. In that case, attack the hanging rook with the king. }
1. Ke6 Rd6+ 2. Ke5 Rd2 { Black will usually adopt a cut-off defense. } 3. Qf7+ Kc6 (3... Kd8 4. Qf4 Re2+ 5. Kd6 Ke8 6. Qg5 { threatening mate on g8 } 6... Kf8 7. Qf5+ Kg7 8. Qg4+ { fork }) 4. Qc4+ { and black has no 3rd rank defense because the black king is off the central ranks } 4... Kd7 5. Qb5+ Kc8 6. Ke6 *


