{ This is an adjacent, non-cutoff rosette position. The two kings are adjacent to each other, the black rook does not cut off the white king from the black king, and the white queen does not cut off the black king from the black rook. In all such rosettes, white plays the same idea: check the king while attacking the rook. }
1. Qc5+ Ke6 2. Ke4 Kd7 (2... Rd1 3. Qc4+ Kd6 4. Qb4+ Kc7 5. Ke5 Rc1 6. Kd5 Rc6 7. Qa5+ Kb7 8. Qb5+ Rb6 9. Qd7+ Kb8 10. Kc5 Ra6 { And we have arrived at the opposite third-rank cutoff rosette position on the edge. }) 3. Qc4 Re6+ 4. Kd5 Rd6+ 5. Ke5 { thorn } *


