{ This position is an adjacent cutoff rosette. The black and white kings are adjacent to each other, the black rook cuts off the white king from the black king, and the white queen cuts off the black king from the black rook. White has a general plan with two exceptions. }
1. Qg6+ { The white queen gives check on the diagonal, driving the king back towards the rook. } 1... Kd5 2. Qe4+ Kd6 3. Qd4+ Rd5 4. Qf6+ Kc5 5. Ke4 { Form the thorn } 5... Rd7 { Black repeats the original rosette. Repeat the same procedure. } 6. Qc3+ Kd6 7. Qe5+ Kc6 8. Qe6+ Rd6 9. Qc4+ Kd7 10. Ke5 Rb6 { Black repeats the original rosette. Repeat the same procedure. } 11. Qf7+ Kc6 12. Qd5+ Kc7 13. Qc5+ Rc6 14. Qe7+ Kb6 15. Kd5 Rc8 { Black repeats the original rosette. Repeat the same procedure. } 16. Qb4+ Kc7 17. Qd6+ Kb7 18. Qd7+ Rc7 19. Qb5+ Kc8 20. Kd6 Rg7 (20... Ra7 21. Qe8+ Kb7 22. Qd7+ Kb8 23. Qd8+ Kb7 24. Qc7+ Ka6 25. Qc6+ Ka5 26. Kc5) 21. Qf5+ Kb7 22. Qe4+ Kb8 23. Kc6 Rb7 24. Qe8+ Ka7 25. Qd8 { Philidor position } *


